{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "עד מדרך כף רגל", :translit "ad midrach kaf regal", :gloss "up to the tread of a foot"} {:he "עד דרך כוכב מיעקב", :translit "ad derech kokhav mi-ya'akov", :gloss "until the way of a star from Jacob"} {:he "עד שיבא זמן שנאמר פורה דרכתי לבדי כף רגל", :translit "ad she-yavo zeman she-ne'emar poreh derachti levadi kaf regal", :gloss "until the time comes that is stated: I have trodden the winepress alone, my foot"} {:he "לעת תמוט דגלם עד שיגיע תדמסנה רגל רגלי עני וגו׳", :translit "la'et tamut degalam ad she-yagi'a tidmasnah regal ragli ani vegomer", :gloss "at the time their banner will fall until my foot arrives, it will trample, my foot, poor, etc."}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Reads 'כף רגל' as a chronotope: Israel's march through Se'ir is bounded by prophetic footsteps"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'כוכב מיעקב' is Balaam's prophecy: 'There shall step forth a star out of Jacob' (Numbers 24:17). 'פורה דרכתי לבדי כף רגלי עני' is Isaiah 63:3: 'I have trodden the winepress alone, and of the peoples there was no man with Me.' The midrash reads Israel's conquest of Se'ir/Edom as deferred until messianic redemption, when the Redeemer's foot treads Edom's winepress (Genesis Rabbah on the rivalry of Jacob and Esau; cf. Rashi on Numbers 24:18 'ואת שעיר ירוש').", :sources ["Numbers 24:17" "Numbers 24:18" "Isaiah 63:3" "Genesis Rabbah"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ירושה לעשו", :translit "yerushah le-'esav", :gloss "an inheritance to Esau"} {:he "בשביל מצות כיבוד", :translit "bishvil mitzvot kibud", :gloss "for the commandment of honoring"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ירושה לעשו", :b "בשביל מצות כיבוד"}], :frame {:text "God charges Israel not to provoke Edom because He has given Mount Se'ir to Esau as an inheritance (Deuteronomy 2:5). The Sifrei on this verse explains that Israel must respect Edom's divinely granted territory. Honoring father and mother is commanded in the Decalogue (Exodus 20:12, Deuteronomy 5:16). By equating 'a possession for Esau' with 'for the commandment of honoring,' Ba'al HaTurim compresses the homictic link between Esau as progenitor of Edom and the filial duty owed to him by his younger brother's descendants.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 2:5" "Exodus 20:12" "Deuteronomy 5:16" "Sifrei Devarim"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Reads 'כף רגל' as a chronotope: Israel's march through Se'ir is bounded by prophetic footsteps", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ירושה לעשו", :a-value 927, :b "בשביל מצות כיבוד", :b-value 922, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:33:42.675906432Z", :model "glm-5.2"}